-# What a save answers the form in the capture frame with. A save that went
-# through touches three places: the head, which counts the amounts up; the
-# frame, which holds the read-only list again -- or the form with the saved
-# values where Speichern und weiter bearbeiten asks for it; and the flash slot
-# of the layout, which names what changed. Values the model refused bring the
-# form back alone, with its errors.
- if @dereg_saved
  = turbo_stream.replace("dereg-summary", partial: "summary")
  = turbo_stream.update("deregistration_capture", partial: @dereg_stay ? "capture_form" : "capture")
  = turbo_stream.update("flash", partial: "layouts/flash", collection: %i[notice warning alert], as: :level)
- else
  = turbo_stream.update("deregistration_capture", partial: "capture_form")
